  "legacy_defects": [
    "unstick's receipt keeps nothing: its allowlist (released, warnings) names lists",
    "unhalt leaves an unsaved empty steer_attempts owner on the cached document, and every later save on the org writes it (docket unhalting-an-agent-leaves-an-unsaved-empty-steer)"
  ],
  "scope": "Legacy boundary of the run-control entry points (P01 F2) on disposable SQLite, per product profile. Every process effect is a spy: halt's cut, interrupts, the killswitch sweep, the warm-pool process control, remote control, the restart launch, the prime arm and cancel, and continue-on's provider read. The doors, the ledger, the halt record, the killswitch latch, the restart-wake sidecar, the receipts, save and reload are real. Legacy conformance evidence only: not a runtime census, not PostgreSQL or Rust qualification."
